IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nz-part2-revision-incorporation`

-- Tests for nz-part2-revision-incorporation.l4 (ss 59 to 66).
-- Every expected value was decided by reading the section quoted beside it BEFORE the module was run.

§ `Section 59 -- Meaning of revision Act and old law`

-- src:410 | revision Act means a revision Bill prepared and certified under subpart 3 of Part 3, once that Bill has been enacted.
#ASSERT `is a revision Act` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is a revision Act` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `is a revision Act` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

-- src:409 | old law, in relation to a revision Act, means the law as expressed in the Acts or parts of Acts repealed by and incorporated in the revision Act
#ASSERT `is old law in relation to the revision Act` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is old law in relation to the revision Act` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `is old law in relation to the revision Act` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 60 -- Revision Act is generally to have same effect as old law`

-- src:411 | 60 Revision Act is generally to have same effect as old law
-- src:412 | A revision Act’s provisions—
-- src:413 | are the provisions of the old law in rewritten form; and
-- src:414 | are intended to have the same effect as the corresponding provisions of the old law.
-- src:415 | This section is subject to section 62.
#ASSERT `a provision of a revision Act is intended to have the same effect as the corresponding old law provision` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `a provision of a revision Act is intended to have the same effect as the corresponding old law provision` TRUE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 61 -- Using old law as interpretation guide for revision Act`

-- src:416 | 61 Using old law as interpretation guide for revision Act
-- src:417 | If the meaning of a provision of a revision Act is unclear or gives rise to absurdity, the wording of the old law that corresponds to the provision must be used to ascertain the meaning of the provision.
#ASSERT `the wording of the corresponding old law must be used to ascertain the meaning` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the wording of the corresponding old law must be used to ascertain the meaning` FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the wording of the corresponding old law must be used to ascertain the meaning` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the wording of the corresponding old law must be used to ascertain the meaning` FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 62 -- Exceptions: when revision Act changes effect of old law`

-- src:418 | 62 Exceptions: when revision Act changes effect of old law
-- src:419 | Section 60 is overridden to the extent that a provision of a revision Act—
-- src:420 | is expressly provided by the revision Act to be intended to change the effect of the old law; or
-- src:421 | has a meaning that is expressly or by necessary implication to a different effect than the corresponding old law provision; or
-- src:422 | is enacted, amended, or repealed by legislation that is not a revision Act (for example, an amendment Act intended to change the effect of the old law).
#ASSERT `section 60 is overridden for the provision of a revision Act` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `section 60 is overridden for the provision of a revision Act` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `section 60 is overridden for the provision of a revision Act` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `section 60 is overridden for the provision of a revision Act` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 63 -- Interpretation (incorporation by reference)`

-- src:426 | material—
-- src:427 | means material referred to in section 64(1); but
-- src:428 | does not include anything incorporated by reference by that material
#ASSERT `is material for sections 64 to 66 and Schedule 2` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is material for sections 64 to 66 and Schedule 2` TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `is material for sections 64 to 66 and Schedule 2` FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- src:429 | written material means material that represents or reproduces words, figures, or symbols—
-- src:430 | in a visible and tangible form by any means and in any medium; or
-- src:431 | in a visible form in any medium by electronic means that enables them to be stored in permanent form and be retrieved and read.
#ASSERT `is written material` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is written material` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is written material` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is written material` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `is written material` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 64 -- Power for secondary legislation to incorporate material by reference`

-- src:433 | This section is sufficient authority for secondary legislation to incorporate 1 or more of the following by reference:
-- src:434 | a standard, framework, code of practice, recommended practice, or requirement of an international organisation or a national organisation:
-- src:435 | a standard, framework, code of practice, recommended practice, or requirement prescribed in any country or jurisdiction, or by any group of countries:
-- src:436 | any other written material that deals with technical matters if it is reasonable to consider that—
-- src:437 | it is impracticable to include the material in the secondary legislation; or
-- src:438 | the material is so large that including it in the secondary legislation will prevent persons to whom the law applies from using or understanding the secondary legislation with reasonable ease.
#ASSERT `section 64 is sufficient authority for secondary legislation to incorporate material that is` `a standard, framework, code of practice, recommended practice or requirement of an international organisation or a national organisation` `when` FALSE `or` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `section 64 is sufficient authority for secondary legislation to incorporate material that is` `a standard, framework, code of practice, recommended practice or requirement prescribed in any country or jurisdiction, or by any group of countries` `when` FALSE `or` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Constituents of the printed items (ruling C): each is on the list whatever the two conditions say.
#ASSERT `section 64 is sufficient authority for secondary legislation to incorporate material that is` `a standard, framework, code of practice, recommended practice or requirement of an international organisation` `when` FALSE `or` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `section 64 is sufficient authority for secondary legislation to incorporate material that is` `a standard, framework, code of practice, recommended practice or requirement of a national organisation` `when` FALSE `or` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `section 64 is sufficient authority for secondary legislation to incorporate material that is` `a standard, framework, code of practice, recommended practice or requirement prescribed in any country` `when` FALSE `or` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `section 64 is sufficient authority for secondary legislation to incorporate material that is` `a standard, framework, code of practice, recommended practice or requirement prescribed in any jurisdiction` `when` FALSE `or` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `section 64 is sufficient authority for secondary legislation to incorporate material that is` `a standard, framework, code of practice, recommended practice or requirement prescribed by any group of countries` `when` FALSE `or` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `section 64 is sufficient authority for secondary legislation to incorporate material that is` `other written material that deals with technical matters` `when` TRUE `or` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `section 64 is sufficient authority for secondary legislation to incorporate material that is` `other written material that deals with technical matters` `when` FALSE `or` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `section 64 is sufficient authority for secondary legislation to incorporate material that is` `other written material that deals with technical matters` `when` TRUE `or` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `section 64 is sufficient authority for secondary legislation to incorporate material that is` `other written material that deals with technical matters` `when` FALSE `or` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `section 64 is sufficient authority for secondary legislation to incorporate material that is` `something else` `when` TRUE `or` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `section 64 is sufficient authority for secondary legislation to incorporate material that is` `something else` `when` FALSE `or` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `section 64 is sufficient authority for secondary legislation to incorporate material that is` `something else` `when` TRUE `or` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- src:439 | For the purposes of this section, secondary legislation incorporates material by reference if the secondary legislation does 1 or more of the following:
-- src:440 | incorporates the material in whole or in part, and with or without modification:
-- src:441 | incorporates amendments to which section 66 applies.
#ASSERT `secondary legislation incorporates material by reference` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `secondary legislation incorporates material by reference` FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `secondary legislation incorporates material by reference` FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- src:442 | Material incorporated by reference in reliance on this section has legal effect as part of the legislation that incorporates the material.
#ASSERT `the material has legal effect as part of the legislation that incorporates it` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the material has legal effect as part of the legislation that incorporates it` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- src:443 | This provision applies in addition to, and does not limit, any of the following:
-- src:444 | any other power in legislation to incorporate material by reference (for example, sections 29 to 32 of the Standards and Accreditation Act 2015):
-- src:445 | the ability of legislation to refer to or incorporate other legislation:
-- src:446 | any rule of law.
#ASSERT `section 64 limits` `any other power in legislation to incorporate material by reference` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `section 64 limits` `the ability of legislation to refer to or incorporate other legislation` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `section 64 limits` `the ability of legislation to refer to other legislation` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `section 64 limits` `the ability of legislation to incorporate other legislation` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `section 64 limits` `any rule of law` EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 65 -- Schedule 2 applies if material incorporated by reference`

-- src:448 | Schedule 2 applies if material is incorporated by reference in reliance on section 64.
#ASSERT `Schedule 2 applies` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Schedule 2 applies` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 66 -- Effect of amendments to material incorporated by reference`

-- src:450 | This section applies if the material incorporated by reference in secondary legislation in reliance on section 64 is amended by the originator of the material after the secondary legislation is made.
-- src:451 | Those amendments have no legal effect as part of the secondary legislation unless—
-- src:452 | they are specifically incorporated by later legislation made in accordance with Schedule 2; or
-- src:453 | amendments to the material are expressly authorised to have that effect by or under another Act.
-- Applies: incorporated in reliance on s 64 and amended by the originator after the secondary legislation was made. Neither exception: no legal effect.
#ASSERT `what effect the amendments to the incorporated material have` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `The amendment has no legal effect as part of the secondary legislation`
#ASSERT `what effect the amendments to the incorporated material have` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Section 66 does not deny the amendment legal effect: an exception applies`
#ASSERT `what effect the amendments to the incorporated material have` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Section 66 does not deny the amendment legal effect: an exception applies`
#ASSERT `what effect the amendments to the incorporated material have` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Section 66 does not deny the amendment legal effect: an exception applies`
-- Does not apply: not incorporated in reliance on s 64, or not amended by the originator after the secondary legislation was made.
#ASSERT `what effect the amendments to the incorporated material have` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Section 66 does not apply`
#ASSERT `what effect the amendments to the incorporated material have` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Section 66 does not apply`

-- src:454 | For the purposes of this section, material is amended if the material or any part of it—
-- src:455 | is amended or replaced; or
-- src:456 | expires or is revoked; or
-- src:457 | otherwise ceases to have effect.
#ASSERT `the material counts as amended for section 66` `it is amended or replaced` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the material counts as amended for section 66` `it is amended` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the material counts as amended for section 66` `it is replaced` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the material counts as amended for section 66` `it expires or is revoked` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the material counts as amended for section 66` `it expires` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the material counts as amended for section 66` `it is revoked` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the material counts as amended for section 66` `it otherwise ceases to have effect` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the material counts as amended for section 66` `it is untouched` EQUALS FALSE
